# TCB --source deploy: temporary backup of functions/ecan-graphql-ws/index.js
# while secrets (WS_PUSH_SECRET/ECAN_JWT_SECRET) are injected as placeholders
# for the cloud build. Should be auto-deleted by trap EXIT on script end.
# Ignored as belt-and-suspenders in case deploy is SIGKILLed.
**/*.tcb-bak

# Design notes whose home is the PRIVATE backend repo (scszcoder/eCan_lambda).
# This repo is public. These carry cost basis, margin, pricing internals, or
# account-security detail (a browser profile is a live seller login), so a
# stray local copy must never be committable here.
docs/VERIFY_ACCOUNT_INFO_API.md
docs/BILLING_METERING_SERVER_TODO.md
docs/MULTI_STORE_MULTI_MACHINE_DESIGN.md

# Fingerprint browser: everything about a local identity stays local.
#
# A profile is a live logged-in seller session plus the proxy credentials it
# egresses through, so none of this may ever be committed. In dev,
# app_info.appdata_path IS the repo root, which is why these land here at all.
# See docs/OWN_FINGERPRINT_BROWSER.md and
# tests/unit/test_browser_profile_stays_local.py.
docs/OWN_FINGERPRINT_BROWSER_PLAN.md

# The registry: proxy endpoints, proxy usernames, exit IPs, vendor profile ids.
browser_profiles.json
browser_profiles.tmp
# The salvaged copy a corrupt registry is moved aside as -- same contents.
browser_profiles.broken-*.json

# User fingerprint presets (the bundled ones under agent/... stay tracked).
fingerprint_profiles/

# Anti-detect vendor credentials: AdsPower api_key, Ziniao username/password.
browser_use_settings.json

# Session directories, if BROWSER_DATA_ROOT is ever pointed inside the repo,
# and the per-profile CDP port file written inside one.
ecan_browser_data/
**/.ecan_cdp.json

# Site-change journal: machine-local forensic history (3-year retention).
# Structural only -- no customer content by construction -- but it is per-machine
# observation data and belongs to the install, not the repo.
drift_journal/
**/drift_journal/
known_shapes.json
resolver_guard.json
**/resolver_guard.json
